subsets/blood_and_immune_upper_slim.json:35038:      \"id\" : \"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel\",\n./__issue_context__.json:2:  \"body\": \"**Description:**\\n\\nWhile attempting to obsolete a term in Protégé following the standard CL protocol, I encountered unexpected behavior: the modification occurred in `merged_import.owl` instead of `cl-edit.owl`.\\n\\nUpon investigation, I found that the term to be obsoleted is also present in `merged_import.owl`, due to an imported `skos:prefLabel` from MBAO. This appears to override the expected editing behavior.\\n\\nI tested removing the term from `merged_import.owl`, and the issue was resolved—only `cl-edit.owl` was modified as expected.\\n\\nSince the `skos:prefLabel` values being imported are typically identical to the term label, this issue could be avoided entirely by excluding `skos:prefLabel` imports from MBAO.\\n\\n**Suggestion:**\\nConsider modifying the import pattern for MBAO to exclude `skos:prefLabel`, as it may be unnecessarily duplicative and is interfering with editing workflows.\",\n./__issue_context__.json:4:  \"title\": \"[Typo/Bug] Obsoleting terms affected by skos:prefLabel import from MBAO\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/blood_and_immune_upper_slim.obo:65:property_value: skos:prefLabel \"cell\" xsd:string\nsrc/ontology/subsets/blood_and_immune_upper_slim.obo:75:property_value: skos:prefLabel \"early embryonic cell (metazoa)\" xsd:string\nsrc/ontology/subsets/blood_and_immune_upper_slim.obo:98:property_value: skos:prefLabel \"stem cell\" xsd:string\nsrc/ontology/subsets/blood_and_immune_upper_slim.obo:153:property_value: skos:prefLabel \"hematopoietic stem cell\" xsd:string\nsrc/ontology/subsets/blood_and_immune_upper_slim.obo:174:property_value: skos:prefLabel \"erythroid progenitor cell\" xsd:string\nsrc/ontology/subsets/blood_and_immune_upper_slim.obo:221:property_value: skos:prefLabel \"multi fate stem cell\" xsd:string\nsrc/ontology/subsets/blood_and_immune_upper_slim.obo:247:property_valu